mber of card points you have you  unlock the ability to play cards to use  them all the different cards you have  have different values so you can build  decks that can potentially bend towards  having a perfectly balanced deck  beginning middle weight you might build  the deck that is entirely weighted  towards having high-end expensive card  points that you only play at the end of  the match or mid-match when you built up  enough card points so you can strategize  in a bunch of different ways and because  you're in it as a team and some of the  core points that you gather will be  shared across the team it's something  where you can have individual  contribution but as a support character  for example you could be pretty focused  on gathering card points for the team  where you might not be out there and  every team fight but the stuff that  you're doing enables the rest of your  team to activate their cards and change  the way they play the game and power up  so when you're taking on board like if  you're unfamiliar maybe with MOBAs and  you're balancing this card system how do  you manage to introduce that to a new  player that's a big part of what we've  been working on over the past few months  we knew going into early access it was  going to be a pretty hardcore experience  I mean not just because it's a MOBA  because we do have some elements that  are a bit of a break from mobile  tradition including the card system so  that's a big piece of it and right now  we're working towards doing a lot to  ease the onboarding process and educate  people for how those different elements  work so before we wrap up I just wanted  to ask you've already touched on quite a  few of these things but looking out to  the future three months six months a  year from now what changes can players  expect beyond new heroes for us we've  gone a lot plan for continuing to evolve  the metagame we're going to be removing  travel mode eventually and replacing it  with new movement mechanics like  teleport beyond that we're also focusing  on new ways of balancing competitive  play and getting into it in different  ways just this week we rolled out draft  mode matchmaking where the game really  begins when you're building up your team  and making decisions based on who picks  what in the very very initial phase of  matchmaking so between that and seeing  how ranked play will evolve as we design  it within the studio those are the types  of things that people have to look  forward to over the next few months and  when so it's in early access at the  moment yep got a basic coming in August  yeah open beta but free open beta will  be August 16 awesome John thank you so  much for joining us guys for more of  your III coverage from this year's show  make sure you stay tuned of course to  gamespot com you're watching the game  spot stage brought to you by airheads  bites  you
 

